#!RuleTest
#test CDISC-SEND-0173 expect=violation domain=LB
#note "Authority: SENDIG 3.1.1 (LBTOXGR / LBTOX: the sponsor is expected to provide the dictionary name and version in define.xml). The define declares the variable in the sponsor's spelling lbtoxgr; a define name is not a library name, so the rule folds it before comparing with LBTOX / LBTOXGR (CIT 1/3). Its CodeListRef points at a CodeList WITHOUT <ExternalCodeList> -> var_external_dictionary(DEFINE) empty -> one violation, reported in the define's spelling. USUBJID and LBTESTCD stay silent."
#library standard=sendig version=3-1-1
#define-xml CDISC-SEND-0173-lowercase-define.xml
#expectViolationCount 1
#expectViolationAt define_variable_name=lbtoxgr
dataset LB
col STUDYID  type=Char
col DOMAIN   type=Char
col USUBJID  type=Char
col LBSEQ    type=Num
col LBTESTCD type=Char
col LBORRES  type=Char
---
S1 | LB | 001 | 1 | GLUC | 5.5
---
